From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brennoflavio <contato@brennoflavio.com.br>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 00:10:05 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] webapi: spoof Mac Chrome navigator platform natively

Return MacIntel from the shared Navigator platform getter instead of
revealing the build host OS. This is desktop Chrome's legacy platform
token on macOS, including Apple silicon; it does not describe the CPU
architecture of the base MacBook Neo / A18 Pro persona.

Preserve the existing native readonly prototype accessor and
WorkerNavigator forwarding. Remove the builtin import used only by the
previous host-OS switch. Client Hint platform and HTTP headers remain
separate work; no new API, configuration or test cases are introduced.

References:
https://github.com/chromium/chromium/blob/main/third_party/blink/renderer/core/execution_context/navigator_base.cc
https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Navigator/platform

Validation: development build and all 1658 existing tests pass. Temporary
diagnostics confirm native descriptors, receiver checks, readonly behavior
and stable MacIntel values in page, worker and frame realms. One reviewer
pass found no issues.
---
 src/browser/webapi/Navigator.zig | 9 +--------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/browser/webapi/Navigator.zig b/src/browser/webapi/Navigator.zig
index fe2010d..fb16d32 100644
--- a/src/browser/webapi/Navigator.zig
+++ b/src/browser/webapi/Navigator.zig
@@ -18,7 +18,6 @@
 // along with this program.  If not, see <https://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.
 
 const std = @import("std");
-const builtin = @import("builtin");
 
 const js = @import("../js/js.zig");
 const Frame = @import("../Frame.zig");
@@ -137,13 +136,7 @@ pub fn getGlobalPrivacyControl(_: *const Navigator) bool {
 }
 
 pub fn getPlatform(_: *const Navigator) []const u8 {
-    return switch (builtin.os.tag) {
-        .macos => "MacIntel",
-        .windows => "Win32",
-        .linux => "Linux x86_64",
-        .freebsd => "FreeBSD",
-        else => "Unknown",
-    };
+    return "MacIntel";
 }
 
 /// Returns whether Java is enabled (always false)
